assessment.why:
Nothing has changed since I paused. The first layer came off, so resuming would print into empty air or onto the stray filament, and none of my adjustments fixes that.

I'm at medium confidence because I can't tell for certain whether the loop at the top of the frame is the dragged ring or the printer's own cable or tubing. The bare sheet, with even the purge line gone, is clear on its own.

The heaters are still on while it waits. The person should:
- remove the loose filament and check the nozzle is clean;
- clean and reseat the textured sheet;
- cancel and restart the print;
- check the first-layer height (live-Z) if it happens again.

A first layer that moves between frames from a fixed camera means it is not stuck to the sheet. The bare sheet after the pause, with even the purge line gone, backs that up. I can't see clearly from here whether the ring is stuck to the nozzle or loose in the chamber, which is why I'm at medium rather than high confidence. Either way, no change to speed, flow, fan or temperature can fix a part that has lifted off, and continuing would only pile filament onto the nozzle. The print stays paused for a person, who needs to:
- remove the loose filament and check the nozzle is clean;
- clean the textured sheet with IPA (or dish soap and water) and check it is seated;
- cancel and restart the print;
- check the first-layer height (live-Z) if it happens again.
